    "locale": "BCP 47 locale the template formats with. Absent, the template chooses it from the currency.",
    "buyer.unit": "The area or team of the buyer the document is addressed to. Leave it out when there is none: never the name of the buyer again, and never a person.",
    "buyer.contact": "The person the document is addressed to, printed on the cover as «Atención: …»: a name, with a role if it helps. Leave it out when there is none.",
    "buyer.logo": "{ path, source }: a local image file and the official HTTPS source it was taken from.",
    "cover.netLabel": "Name of the net printed on the cover, in place of the one of the template: «Valor neto del proyecto», «Valor neto del programa». A text, never an amount.",
    "schedule.note": "A line next to the title of the calendar of the work. Leave it out when it would only say what any quote implies, such as that the work starts when agreed.",
    "pricing.taxLabel": "Name of the tax when it is not the default of the template.",
    "pricing.monthly": "{ months, note }: prints the monthly equivalent of the totals. A count of months, not an amount.",
    "lines.<key>.detail": "Second line of a concept. A concept whose net changes over the term says which months each line covers unless a detail is given.",
    "lines.<key>.courtesy": "true prints a line the quote waives completely as a courtesy: net zero and its reference value. Only for the keys listed under `waived`, with their label, detail and group like any line; a waived key that is not marked prints nothing.",
    "combine": "[{ keys, label, unit, detail?, group?, per? }]: prints the keys of `keys` as one line, a price for the whole of them («1 programa», «1 proyecto», «1 servicio»): quantity 1 of `unit`, no unit value, and for net the sum the quote froze for those keys over the whole term. One key alone may be combined (a fee printed as a programme price instead of months). A key goes in one combination at most and then has no entry in `lines`; a key the quote waives cannot be combined. Without it every key prints folded by months, as listed under `lines`. With `per: \"period\"` (default `\"term\"`) the keys are added up inside each month instead, and the months fold like a single key: «6 meses» at the sum of one month, with a line per stretch of months when that sum changes. For a price agreed as one amount a month with everything in it (a start-up included). The unit is the month, so such an entry gives no `unit`.",
    "options": "{ <key>: { label, unit, detail? } } for each option passed with `--option <key>=<artifact.json>`: its name, the unit its price is read in («al mes», «por campaña») and an optional second line. Exactly the options passed; the price of each is the net of one period of its own frozen quote.",
    "optionsTexts": "{ title, note } of the block of options. Only with options.",
    "paymentMilestones": "The list `compose schedule --milestones` takes: [{ id, label, share, periodId | when }]. Shares add up to 1; the amounts are derived from the net. Each milestone needs periodId or when. When the quote has an exclusive tax rate, each milestone is printed with its part of the frozen tax and its total.",
    "paymentScheduleTexts": "{ title, note } of the payment calendar. Only with paymentMilestones. Without a note, a calendar of nets says that its amounts carry no tax, and one whose milestones carry their tax prints none."
